From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:16:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the world's and the entities' random numbers without a
 compare-and-set

java.util.Random advances its 48 bits of state with a CAS on an AtomicLong so
that two threads cannot be handed the same number. The tick loop does not need
that, and PandaSpigot points every entity at one shared generator, so that CAS
is one of the most repeated read-modify-writes in the tick.

SnapshotRandom already reimplemented java.util.Random's generator over a plain
long, for a different reason - decoration needs to rewind the sequence - so the
generator moves down into FastRandom and SnapshotRandom keeps only the rewind.
Entity.SHARED_RANDOM and World.random now use FastRandom.

The numbers are unchanged: same 48-bit LCG, same scramble in setSeed, same
shift in next(bits), and every other method of java.util.Random is defined in
terms of next(bits). Checked against java.util.Random over seven seeds and
20,000 draws each of nextInt, nextInt(bound) both power-of-two and not,
nextDouble, nextLong and nextBoolean.

What is given up is thread safety on those two generators. The state is a
single long, so a racing draw returns a stale number rather than breaking the
generator, and nothing in the server draws from either off the server thread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

